A||N||13||DaRkLoRD||Status of Fiero Project business cards||||4||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||06-26-2000||10:47 PM||||Several of you have emailed me asking about the status of the cards.. a few of you have even offered to send me some money to put towards the cost, and that's awesome.. you'll be getting a big stack of them for that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Monkeyman had an excellent suggestion of listing some Fiero businesses on the back, which is not only an excellent way for Fiero owners to locate parts and aftermarket accessories for their cars, it's also extremely cheap advertising for the Fiero vendors.. I've decided to have several versions of the cards, the cards going to the southwest will have vendors from the southwest.. (such as the Fiero Shop), and ones in southern Canada or the northeast USA could have vendors such as RSM listed. (just an example, I have not contacted them yet about this, but I plan to shortly.) So far FieroDave and Fieroshop have said they're interested, and I think SuperX?<P>Those of you who have offered to help, or have sent some money already, thank you... if I can get just a couple more people to advertise, I'll be able to offer the cards at little or no cost to forum members..<P>so, if you have any suggestions of Fiero businesses that would be in having their name, phone number, email/web address printed on the back of a few hundred cards that will be shipped all across north america, for just $30.. let them know about this offer.. I really appreciate all the help and suggestions you people have given me in the past.. thanks. you guys are great..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||06-26-2000||11:05 PM||||Steve, there  also may be some Clubs that  want some advertising??  I know some forum members are starting NEW Clubs this may give them the boost they need.<P>Just a thought?<P>DXR_DAD<BR>Fiero Project Member  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||06-26-2000||11:37 PM||||Good idea!!<P>email me at  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  if you're interested in advertising, whether for a club, business, etc.. I'll get back to you ASAP!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||06-27-2000||03:43 AM||||with this focoa thing coming up here i've just been scibbling notes and leaving them on fieros if i get a chance. i mention the meet, the forum ,and my email addy. i keep hoping someone shows up here.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-27-2000||01:57 PM||||Steve--If you only advertise the SW businesses in the SW, etc. how will those of us in other parts of the US/Canada get the site addys for the rest of the countries?  What I'm trying to say is, what happens if I need to contact RSM or Ed Parks (talked to him, yet or what about Bob Steiger/Twin Lakes Fiero?)?  Or is room/size a factor?<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||06-27-2000||02:35 PM||||Monkeyman, yes, space is a big factor on the cards.. in order to give enough room for each business to list their name, phone number, a few words saying what they sell/what service they provide and a web and email address.. it's at least 2 lines each.<P>You have a very good point though.. I'm sure a lot of the vendors deal mostly with more local people than the bigger companies like the fiero store, which ships nationwide all the time.. I can't fit all of the advertising on all the cards.. so how do I get all of the major vendors on all the cards, but still have room for a few of the smaller ones?? shrinking the text any more isn't really an option, as then it would be too hard to read. thanks for bringing this point up...<P>anyone have any suggestions on what I should do???||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||06-27-2000||08:13 PM||||I think the idea of giving space to local vendors is a great idea. A couple of different ideas can help facilitate that while still allowng space for nationwide ads. First, (and this idea could be a total wash based on the stage of development that you are in)is make the card in a folded "greeting card" style with major $pon$or$ on the outside, with smaller regional ads on the inside. Inside graphic b&w, outsde nice slick color. Might test fit to see if it will slide in to the door pull (without setting off alarms).<BR>Another idea is to charge different amounts based on distribution and size/placement of ads. Here in Oklahoma we have Design 1. Great candidate for national ad. We also have local dealerships that sponsor our club functions and give discounts on parts. Which would be basically useless to anyone outside Oklahoma.<P>Anyhow my post is far too long but I do have other ideas that I coud share with you in private email if you are interested.  Marketing was kinda my thing in college so I'm just kinda brimmin with good and bad ideas. Let's brainstorm!||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||06-27-2000||08:30 PM||||Steve, I think Stimpy is on the right track<BR>I sent you a sample of the cards I did (not as good as a pro) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I used blank invitations<BR>and ran them through my laser printer, tent fold style gave me 4 nice size spots, They evan have a picture of my car on them and a big Pontiac logo. The Pennock Forum card is printed on the  front. <P>Let me know what you think of them.||||reg||14
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||06-27-2000||10:11 PM||||Stimpy, feel free to email me with any more ideas.. the suggestion about the folded cards is a bit out of my price range.. about 4x the cost of normal cards actually.. and it'd cost a lot more to ship.. I bet we could come up with an idea that will work great though.. send me an email and we can do some brainstorming.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||87ECO5||06-29-2000||09:40 AM||||Steve - very rough idea ...<P>What about setting up an advertising page off of fieroproject.com and putting it's URL on the card?  You've got a lot more room to work with.  The downside is you single out those that don't have Internet access.<P>Just a <I>QUICK</I> thought ...||||reg||5
